Source: libglvnd
Section: libs
Maintainer: crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.3
# Упаковка взята из Debian (libglvnd 1.7.0-3) и переработана:
#   * GLX и GL не публикуются: GLX есть X11-протокол, а GL у нас не
#     собирается. OpenGL ES 1 и 2 публикуются - они не про X11: в
#     src/meson.build блоки subdir('GLX')/subdir('GL') стоят под
#     if with_glx, а GLESv1/GLESv2 под независимыми опциями gles1/gles2.
#     Проверено сборкой: libGLESv1_CM.so.1 и libGLESv2.so.2 собираются при
#     -Dglx=disabled, в NEEDED только libGLdispatch.so.0 и libc.so.6, строк
#     libX11.so.6/libGLX.so.0/libGL.so.1 нет. Из 14 бинарных пакетов Debian
#     остаются семь: libglvnd0, libglvnd-core-dev, libegl1, libegl-dev,
#     libgles1, libgles2, libgles-dev;
#   * X11-пакеты убраны из Build-Depends (libx11-dev, libxext-dev, x11proto-dev,
#     xauth, xvfb), тесты не собираются;
#   * из libegl-dev убраны Depends: libgl-dev, libgles-dev, libglx-dev,
#     libopengl-dev, а из libgles-dev - Depends: libgl-dev. Все они публикует
#     glvnd, а тот тянет libgl1-mesa-dev и libglx-mesa0, которые пинят libgbm1
#     версии trixie. Из-за этого libegl-dev становился неразрешимым рядом с
#     нашей mesa. В libgles-dev зависимость от libgl-dev в Debian и вовсе
#     надумана: в его .install нет ни одного файла GL, она нужна только ради
#     GL-заголовков. Разбор - в packages/libglvnd/README.md;
#   * dbgsym-пакеты не собираются (общее правило scripts/build-package.sh).
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               meson,
               pkgconf,
               python3-setuptools
Homepage: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/glvnd/libglvnd
Vcs-Git: https://salsa.debian.org/xorg-team/lib/libglvnd.git
Vcs-Browser: https://salsa.debian.org/xorg-team/lib/libglvnd.git

Package: libglvnd0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: Vendor neutral GL dispatch library
 This is an implementation of the vendor-neutral dispatch layer for arbitrating
 OpenGL API calls between multiple vendors on a per-screen basis.
 .
 This package provides libGLdispatch, the dispatching half of the library. It
 is needed by libegl1 and is not useful on its own.

Package: libglvnd-core-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libglvnd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: Vendor neutral GL dispatch library -- core development files
 Internal headers and the pkg-config file of the vendor-neutral dispatch
 layer.

Package: libegl1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libglvnd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: GL dispatch library runtime for EGL
 This is a runtime package for EGL, the vendor-neutral dispatch layer. The
 window-system platform for X11 is not built here, so libEGL.so.1 depends on
 no window-system library at all.

Package: libegl-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libegl1 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libglvnd-core-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: GL dispatch library runtime and development files for EGL
 This package provides the EGL headers, egl.pc and libEGL.so needed to build
 against EGL.
 .
 The GL, GLES, GLX and OpenGL variants of this package are not published
 here: they require X11 and GL, neither of which is part of this repository.

Package: libgles1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libglvnd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: GL dispatch library runtime for OpenGL ES 1.x
 This is a runtime package for OpenGL ES 1.x, the vendor-neutral dispatch
 layer. It needs no window-system library: GLX is not built here.

Package: libgles2
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libglvnd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: GL dispatch library runtime for OpenGL ES 2.x and 3.x
 This is a runtime package for OpenGL ES 2.x and 3.x, the vendor-neutral
 dispatch layer. It needs no window-system library: GLX is not built here.

Package: libgles-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libegl-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 libgles1 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libgles2 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libopengl-dev,
 ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: GL dispatch library runtime and development files for OpenGL ES
 This package provides the OpenGL ES headers (GLES/, GLES2/, GLES3/), the
 glesv1_cm.pc and glesv2.pc pkg-config files, and libGLESv1_CM.so and
 libGLESv2.so needed to build against OpenGL ES.
 .
 Unlike Debian's package it does not depend on libgl-dev: that dependency
 exists only for the GL headers, which this package does not contain. See
 packages/libglvnd/README.md.

Package: libopengl0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libglvnd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: Vendor neutral GL dispatch library -- OpenGL support
 This is the vendor-neutral dispatch layer for OpenGL without GLX. It needs
 no window-system library and is what gstreamer1.0-gl-prototypes-1.0.pc
 resolves its "opengl" requirement against.

Package: libopengl-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libopengl0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: same
Description: Vendor neutral GL dispatch library -- OpenGL development files
 This package provides the opengl.pc pkg-config file and libOpenGL.so needed
 to build against OpenGL without GLX.
